<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23204" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-findo</span></b> , fĭdi, fissum,
		3, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to cut into</i>, <i>to cleave</i>
				(<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">telluri sulcos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 4, 33</span></i>
			; so <b>poet.</b>, sulcos, for <i>to plough up</i>, <i>make by
			sailing</i>, <i><span class="en">id. A. 5, 142</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">silvam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					50, 66</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">volat cava pinus infinditque salum,</span>”
				<i>cuts through</i>, <i>sails through</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 1, 687</span></i>
			.</div>
